From aeb4ebcd5229188669fd7cefe42c945d232e653d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:46:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/76] perf(pcs): parallel batched linear quotients for
 Shplonk and KZG

Shplonk's batched quotient Q(X) = sum_j nu^j (f_j(X) - v_j)/(X - x_j) was built by copying each
claim polynomial, dividing it serially with factor_roots and add_scaled-ing it into Q. KZG's
quotient was a copy plus a serial factor_roots.

add_batched_linear_quotients computes the same polynomial with the descending synthetic-division
recurrence q_i = p_{i+1} + x q_{i+1}, split into work-balanced chunks: a Horner pass gives each
chunk's boundary value, then every chunk runs the recurrence and accumulates nu_j q_i directly
into the output, with no per-claim copies. Exact division is still asserted (p_0 - v + x q_0 = 0).

Shplonk's partially evaluated quotient G = Q - sum_j s_j f_j is applied in one add_scaled_batch
pass, a Gemini fold polynomial opened at +-r^{2^l} entering once with the sum of its two factors,
and G is moved rather than copied into the returned claim.
